<div class="note">
  <p class="note__label">Read this first</p>
  <p>Fees, payment deadlines and what each category includes have not been set. This form does not sell you anything and does not hold a place. It registers your interest so the secretariat can contact you directly the moment the details are confirmed — and so it knows how many of each category to plan for.</p>
</div>

<h2>The six categories</h2>

<ul class="classes">
{% for c in summit.registrationCategories %}
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__code">Class {{ loop.index }}</span>
    <span class="class-row__name">{{ c.name }}</span>
    <p>{{ c.blurb }}</p>
  </li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>What is set, and what is not</h2>

<dl class="spec">
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">Dates</dt>
    <dd class="value">{{ summit.dates.display }}</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">City</dt>
    <dd class="value">{{ summit.location.city }}, {{ summit.location.country }}</dd>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">Venue</dt>
    <dd class="value"><span class="value--pending">To be announced</span></dd>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">Fees</dt>
    <dd class="value"><span class="value--pending">To be announced</span></dd>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">Registration deadline</dt>
    <dd class="value"><span class="value--pending">To be announced</span></dd>
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <dt class="label">What each category includes</dt>
    <dd class="value"><span class="value--pending">To be announced</span></dd>
  </div>
</dl>

{% include "components/form-registration.njk" %}

<h2>What happens next</h2>

<ol>
  <li>You get an email confirming the secretariat has your details. It arrives immediately.</li>
  <li>Your entry is recorded against the category you chose.</li>
  <li>When fees, the venue and the programme are confirmed, the secretariat contacts you before the public announcement.</li>
</ol>

<p>If you would rather exhibit or partner than attend, those go through <a href="/exhibition/">Exhibition</a> and <a href="/sponsorship/">Partnership</a> instead — different forms, different information needed.</p>
